CoordSys: one shared material bound by rprims to *different* cameras

Two grids reference the same </gridTemplate> (so each has its own projector
camera inside it) but they all bind a single shared MaterialX material
</mtl/projected> - one node graph shared by both rprims. Each grid binds the
'map_proj' coordinate system to its own projector camera.

Arnold resolves named coordinate spaces globally by camera node name, so the
single shared "space" input cannot serve both cameras: arnold-usd keeps the base
material for the first binding and re-translates a per-rprim variant for the
conflicting one, so each grid projects from its own camera. Without this, both
grids would project from a single camera (the second grid's gradient shifted).

The projector cameras live inside the grid template (as in test_13221) so the
coordinate-system camera resolves identically under the legacy scene delegate
(hydra) and the scene index (hydra2).

See #32 / ARNOLD-13221

author: cyril.pichard

PARAMS: {'scene':'test.usda', 'kick_params':'-c /Cameras/renderCamera'}
